{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2150-10-23 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. Johnson. I'm Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. You came in today because your dialysis access in the left arm stopped working, is that right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2150-10-23 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, doc. At my last session, they couldn’t get it to work. But I didn’t feel any pain or anything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2150-10-23 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common. We checked with an ultrasound, and it showed a clot in your graft. That’s why it wasn’t working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2150-10-23 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A clot? Like a blood clot? Is that dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2150-10-23 15:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be if it blocks the access. But we’ve placed a temporary catheter in your groin so you can still get dialysis. That’s already done, and you’re all set for tonight’s session."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2150-10-23 15:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. I didn’t even feel that. But will the clot go away?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2150-10-23 15:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We plan to remove it tomorrow with a procedure called a thrombectomy. It’s done by a specialist using imaging to guide tools into the graft and clear the clot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2150-10-23 15:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2150-10-23 15:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get some medication to keep you comfortable. You’ll be awake but relaxed. Most patients feel only pressure, not pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2150-10-23 15:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. And my potassium was high earlier, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2150-10-23 15:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it was very high, which can be dangerous for the heart. But we gave you some treatments, and you’ve already had two hours of dialysis. Your levels are much better now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2150-10-23 15:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve had that before. My feet are bothering me again though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2150-10-23 15:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know your neuropathy pain can be tough. We’ll keep your gabapentin and oxycodone going. Let us know if it gets worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2150-10-24 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Today’s the day for the clot removal. You’ll be going to radiology in a few hours. Any questions before we start?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2150-10-24 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is there a chance something could go wrong?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2150-10-24 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Like any procedure, there are risks. One is that a small piece of clot could break off and go to the lungs. But the team is ready for that and will monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2150-10-24 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds scary."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2150-10-24 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But it’s rare, and if it happens, it often resolves on its own. We won’t use blood thinners because of your history of stomach bleeds, but we’ll watch you carefully."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2150-10-24 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, Mr. Johnson. You’re back from the procedure. It went well — they cleared the clot and opened up the graft. You have good blood flow now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2150-10-24 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember feeling short of breath for a bit… and some chest pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2150-10-24 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that happened. The radiologist thinks a small clot may have gone to your lung — a minor pulmonary embolism. But your oxygen recovered quickly, and you’re stable now. No treatment is needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2150-10-24 13:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2150-10-24 13:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You were a bit groggy afterward from the pain meds, but you’re alert now. We’ll keep an eye on your oxygen and blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2150-10-24 13:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. My feet still hurt, but not as bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2150-10-24 13:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep your pain meds going, but we’ll be cautious so you don’t get too sleepy. Your neuropathy is chronic, so we’re not changing anything there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2150-10-24 19:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your dialysis went well this afternoon. Your graft is working, and we’ll remove the groin catheter soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2150-10-24 19:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Can I go home tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2150-10-24 19:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We want to make sure your blood pressure stays stable. You had a drop last night — probably from fasting and dialysis — but it’s back to normal now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2150-10-24 19:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve always run a little low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2150-10-24 19:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and that’s okay as long as you feel fine. We’ll check one more dialysis session tomorrow, and if all looks good, you can go back to your facility."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2150-10-25 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news — your labs are stable, your graft is working, and your oxygen is 100% on your usual 2 liters. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2150-10-25 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What about my CPAP? I haven’t been using it at the facility."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2150-10-25 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re restarting it. You have sleep apnea, and using CPAP helps your heart and oxygen levels. Your sleep specialist wants to see you for a mask fitting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2150-10-25 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try. But it’s uncomfortable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2150-10-25 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll work with the sleep team to get it adjusted. It’s important, especially after what happened with your oxygen during the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2150-10-25 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. And my heart medicine — diltiazem — is that still okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2150-10-25 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s still prescribed. You’re not on blood thinners because of your past stomach bleeds, but the diltiazem helps control your rhythm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2150-10-25 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my diabetes meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2150-10-25 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll keep your insulin — glargine and the sliding scale. Your blood sugar is a bit high, but stable. We’ll leave adjustments to your outpatient team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2150-10-25 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And when do I see the cardiologist?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2150-10-25 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You have an appointment scheduled for next week. Also, don’t forget your sleep specialist. We’re sending instructions to your facility."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2150-10-25 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thank you, doc."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2150-10-25 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. One last thing — weigh yourself every morning. If you gain more than three pounds, call your doctor. That could mean fluid buildup."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2150-10-25 09:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that. I remember from last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2150-10-25 09:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. And if you have trouble breathing on your usual oxygen, let someone know right away. Otherwise, you’re doing well and ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2150-10-25 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel ready. Thanks for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2150-10-25 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Our pleasure. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2150-10-25 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before discharge. Your graft has a good thrill and bruit — that means it’s working well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2150-10-25 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I can feel it pulsing now. Much better than before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2150-10-25 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. That’s what we want. Keep an eye on it — if it ever stops pulsing or becomes painful, let your team know."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2150-10-25 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2150-10-25 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs show your potassium is stable, and your kidney function is as expected for someone on dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2150-10-25 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No more emergency dialysis, I hope."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2150-10-25 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not if we can help it. Keeping your graft healthy is key. That means no pressure on the arm and checking the site daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2150-10-25 10:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll be careful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2150-10-25 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. And keep taking your sevelamer with meals — it helps control your phosphorus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2150-10-25 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I remember that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2150-10-25 10:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Alright, everything looks good. We’ll get the discharge papers ready. You should be on your way within a few hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2150-10-25 10:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate it. I’ll follow up with the specialists."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2150-10-25 10:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Take care, Mr. Johnson."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2150-10-23 14:39:00",
    "admission_end": "2150-10-25 17:02:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A man with end-stage renal disease, type 2 diabetes, chronic heart failure, atrial fibrillation, and a history of gastrointestinal bleeding was admitted after his left upper extremity arteriovenous graft failed due to thrombosis. He presented from dialysis with no thrill or bruit but no pain or infection signs. He was hyperkalemic on arrival and received emergent dialysis via a temporary femoral catheter. The next day, he underwent a thrombectomy with mechanical and chemical thrombolysis, which successfully restored graft patency. The procedure was briefly complicated by transient hypoxia and chest pain, attributed to a small pulmonary embolism, which resolved without intervention. He remained alert and stable, with resolution of hyperkalemia and successful dialysis through the restored graft. He was restarted on CPAP for obstructive sleep apnea and discharged to extended care with follow-up appointments in cardiology and sleep medicine. His medications, including insulin, diltiazem, and neuropathy regimen, were continued without major changes.",
    "problems": [
      "Other complications due to renal dialysis device, implant, and graft",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Iatrogenic pulmonary embolism and infarction",
      "Hyperpotassemia",
      "Chronic diastolic heart failure",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Atrial fibrillation",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult)(pediatric)",
      "Other dependence on machines, supplemental oxygen"
    ]
  }
}
